      "formation": "2nd Division, Imperial Guard",
      "side": "French",
      "summary": "With Kutuzov's army closing on the road at Krasnoi, Napoleon sent the Young Guard out in the night of 16 November to attack the Russians at Uvarovo; they drove Golitsyn's men back, and on the 17th stood in the snow before the town to hold the road open for Davout, losing half their strength.",
